TIP:  (Am/G) is just (Am) with your pinky added to note <g> at the 1st string/3rd fret and is only played for one strum in the second half of the intro.

TIP:  The chord changes are a little “slippery” in places so it will help to anticipate the (Am) (G) (F) (E) chord progression.  Also notice many chords that start a line come in a beat early and are shown at the end of the preceding line.

TIP:  In the first two lines of some of the verses the movement from (G) to (F) to (E) is quick and will catch you out if you don’t anticipate it.


